From: EVE build <builder@projecteve.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] aot: compile without helper error checks

bpftrace 0.23.3 compiles helper error checks into every program by
default (0.20.3 did not, and refused -k together with --aot), but the
helper error information is not part of the AOT payload: it is left out
of RequiredResources::serialize. When a helper fails at run time, for
example delete() of a key that was never inserted, the runtime formats
the event with a default HelperErrorInfo, whose helper name is a null
string, which puts its output stream into the failed state: nothing is
printed from then on, and the JSON output ends in a broken line.

Compile ahead-of-time programs without helper error checks, as 0.20.3
did; the runtime has no way to report them anyway.

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index 5796a7e..2941986 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -664,6 +664,14 @@ Args parse_args(int argc, char* argv[])
     exit(1);
   }
 
+  // The same holds for the default level: the helper error information is
+  // not part of the AOT payload (see RequiredResources::serialize), so the
+  // runtime cannot report a failed helper; it would print a broken message
+  // and lose every output after it. Compile ahead-of-time programs without
+  // helper error checks, as bpftrace 0.20.3 did.
+  if (args.build_mode == BuildMode::AHEAD_OF_TIME)
+    args.helper_check_level = 0;
+
   if (args.listing) {
     // Expect zero or one positional arguments
     if (optind == argc) {
